->values([
  'sid' => '46',
  'langcode' => 'en',
  'type' => 'help_search',
  'data' => ' managing content moderation workflows what is a content moderation workflow  on some sites new content and content revisions need to be moderated  that is they need to pass through several states before becoming visible to site visitors the collection of states and the definition of the transitions between states is known as a workflow  for example new content might start out in a draft state and then might need to pass through several review states before it becomes published on the live site the core software allows you to configure workflows in which each transition has an associated permission that can be granted to a particular role see configuring workflows for more information users with sufficient permissions can change the workflow state of a particular entity see moving content between workflow states for more information overview of content moderation workflows the core content moderation module allows you to expand on core software s unpublished and published states for content it allows you to have a published version that is live but have a separate working copy that is undergoing review before it is published this is achieved by using workflows to apply different states and transitions to entities as needed the core workflows module allows you to manage workflows with states and transitions see the related topics listed below for specific tasks and background information additional resources online documentation about content moderation ',
  'reindex' => '0',
])
->values([
  'sid' => '46',
  'langcode' => 'es',
  'type' => 'help_search',
  'data' => ' managing content moderation workflows  que es un flujo de trabajo de moderacion de contenido  on some sites new content and content revisions need to be moderated  that is they need to pass through several states before becoming visible to site visitors the collection of states and the definition of the transitions between states is known as a workflow  for example new content might start out in a draft state and then might need to pass through several review states before it becomes published on the live site el software principal le permite configurar flujos de trabajo en los que cada transicion tiene un permiso asociado que se puede otorgar a un rol en particular consulte configuring workflows para obtener mas informacion los usuarios con suficientes permisos pueden cambiar el estado del flujo de trabajo de una entidad en particular consulte moving content between workflow states para obtener mas informacion descripcion general de los flujos de trabajo de moderacion de contenido the core content moderation module allows you to expand on core software s unpublished and published states for content it allows you to have a published version that is live but have a separate working copy that is undergoing review before it is published this is achieved by using workflows to apply different states and transitions to entities as needed the core workflows module allows you to manage workflows with states and transitions see the related topics listed below for specific tasks and background information recursos adicionales documentacion en linea sobre moderacion de contenido ',
  'reindex' => '0',
])
->values([
  'sid' => '47',
  'langcode' => 'en',
  'type' => 'help_search',
  'data' => ' viewing drupal announcements what are drupal announcements  a feed of announcements about the drupal project and drupal association programs the purpose of this feed is to provide a channel for outreach directly to drupal site owners this content must be highly relevant to site owners interests serve the strategic goals of the project and or promote the sustainability of the project and the drupal association the module sources its content from a json feed generated from here  the governance policy for the content is documented here  how can i see the announcements in my site  if you have the toolbar module enabled you will see a direct link to them in the toolbar if the toolbar module is not enabled the content can always be accessed in the announcements page who can see the announcements  users with the view official announcements related to drupal permission can view drupal announcements additional resources announcement module overview ',
  'reindex' => '0',
])
->values([
  'sid' => '47',
  'langcode' => 'es',
  'type' => 'help_search',
  'data' => ' viewing drupal announcements what are drupal announcements  a feed of announcements about the drupal project and drupal association programs the purpose of this feed is to provide a channel for outreach directly to drupal site owners this content must be highly relevant to site owners interests serve the strategic goals of the project and or promote the sustainability of the project and the drupal association the module sources its content from a json feed generated from here  the governance policy for the content is documented here  how can i see the announcements in my site  if you have the toolbar module enabled you will see a direct link to them in the toolbar if the toolbar module is not enabled the content can always be accessed in the anuncios page who can see the announcements  users with the view official announcements related to drupal permission can view drupal announcements recursos adicionales announcement module overview ',
  'reindex' => '0',
])
->values([
  'sid' => '48',
  'langcode' => 'en',
  'type' => 'help_search',
  'data' => ' configuring workflows goal create or edit a workflow with various workflow states for example concept   archived  etc for moderating content see managing content moderation workflows for more information on workflows who can configure a workflow  users with workflows permissions  typically administrators can configure workflows see permissions  administer workflows to configure workflows permissions steps make a plan for the new workflow decide which workflow states you need for example  concept   review  and final  decide on the settings for each state  label  the state name published  if checked when content reaches this state it will be made visible on the site to users with permission  default revision  if checked when content reaches this state it will become the default revision of the content published content is automatically the default revision decide which state content should be created in decide on the list of allowed transitions between states for example you might want a transition between concept and review  each transition has a label for example the concept to review transition might be labeled review concept decide which roles should have permissions to make each transition see managing user accounts and site visitors for an overview of roles and permissions decide which entity types and subtypes the workflow should apply to only entity types that support revisions are possible to define workflows for see managing content structure for more information on content entities and fields to implement your plan in the manage administrative menu navigate to configuration   workflow   workflows  a list of workflows is shown including the default workflow editorial that you can adapt click add workflow  enter a name in the label field select content moderation from the workflow type field and click save  verify that the states list matches your planned states you can add missing states by clicking add a new state  you can edit or delete states by clicking edit or delete under operations  if the delete option is not available you will first need to delete any transitions to or from this state verify that the transitions list matches your plan you can add missing transitions by clicking add a new transition  you can edit or delete transitions by clicking edit or delete under operations  under this workflow applies to   find the entity type that you want this workflow to apply to such as content revisions content block revisions or taxonomy term revisions click select  check the entity subtypes that you want to apply the workflow to for example you might choose to apply your workflow to the page content type but not to article  click save  under workflow settings  select the default moderation state for new content click save to save your workflow follow the steps in modifying the permissions for a role to assign permissions for each transition to roles the permissions are listed under the content moderation section there is one permission for each transition in each workflow optionally recommended create a view for your custom workflow to provide a page for content editors to see what content needs to be moderated you can do this if the views ui module is installed by following the steps in the related creating a new view topic listed below under related topics  when creating the view under view settings   show  select the revision data type you configured the workflow for and be sure to display the workflow state field in your view  ',
  'reindex' => '0',
])
->values([
  'sid' => '48',
  'langcode' => 'es',
  'type' => 'help_search',
  'data' => ' configuring workflows objetivo cree o edite un flujo de trabajo con varios estados de flujo de trabajo por ejemplo  concepto   archivado  etc para moderar contenido consulte managing content moderation workflows para obtener mas informacion sobre los flujos de trabajo  quien puede configurar un flujo de trabajo  users with workflows permissions  typically administrators can configure workflows see permissions  administrar flujos de trabajo to configure workflows permissions pasos haga un plan para el nuevo flujo de trabajo decide which workflow states you need for example  concept   review  and final  decida la configuracion de cada estado  label  the state name published  if checked when content reaches this state it will be made visible on the site to users with permission  default revision  if checked when content reaches this state it will become the default revision of the content published content is automatically the default revision decide which state content should be created in decide on the list of allowed transitions between states for example you might want a transition between concept and review  each transition has a label for example the concept to review transition might be labeled review concept decide which roles should have permissions to make each transition see managing user accounts and site visitors for an overview of roles and permissions decide which entity types and subtypes the workflow should apply to only entity types that support revisions are possible to define workflows for see managing content structure for more information on content entities and fields to implement your plan in the manage administrative menu navigate to configuration   workflow   flujos de trabajo  a list of workflows is shown including the default workflow editorial that you can adapt haga clic en agregar flujo de trabajo  enter a name in the label field select content moderation from the workflow type field and click save  verify that the states list matches your planned states you can add missing states by clicking add a new state  you can edit or delete states by clicking edit or delete under operations  if the delete option is not available you will first need to delete any transitions to or from this state verify that the transitions list matches your plan you can add missing transitions by clicking add a new transition  you can edit or delete transitions by clicking edit or delete under operations  under this workflow applies to   find the entity type that you want this workflow to apply to such as content revisions content block revisions or taxonomy term revisions click select  check the entity subtypes that you want to apply the workflow to for example you might choose to apply your workflow to the page content type but not to article  pulse guardar  under workflow settings  select the default moderation state for new content haga clic en guardar para guardar su flujo de trabajo follow the steps in modifying the permissions for a role to assign permissions for each transition to roles the permissions are listed under the moderacion de contenido section there is one permission for each transition in each workflow optionally recommended create a view for your custom workflow to provide a page for content editors to see what content needs to be moderated you can do this if the views ui module is installed by following the steps in the related creating a new view topic listed below under related topics  when creating the view under view settings   show  select the revision data type you configured the workflow for and be sure to display the workflow state field in your view  ',
  'reindex' => '0',
])
->values([
  'sid' => '49',
  'langcode' => 'en',
  'type' => 'help_search',
  'data' => ' moving content between workflow states goal change the workflow state of a particular entity see managing content moderation workflows for an overview of workflows and managing content structure for an overview of content entities who can change workflow states  users with content moderation permissions can change workflow states there are separate permissions for each transition see permissions  content moderation to configure content moderation permissions steps find the entity that you want to moderate in either the content moderation view page if you created one or the appropriate administrative page for managing that type of entity such as the administration page for content items see content click edit to edit the entity at the bottom of the page select the new workflow state under change to  and click save   ',
